# API Clean Architecture

Never call Dio from widgets, screens, BLoCs, or Cubits.

```text
Presentation → BLoC/Cubit → UseCase → Repository (interface)
  → RepositoryImpl → Remote DataSource → Dio → Backend
```

## Config and auth

- Base URL lives only in `AppConfig` (`lib/core/config/app_config.dart`). Support Dev/Staging/Production via dart-define, not scattered URLs.
- Follow Postman’s auth. Store the login token and attach it via the **Dio interceptor**. Do not set `Authorization` in each feature. Never log passwords or tokens.

## Models vs domain

Backend JSON models stay in Data. Domain entities must not depend on Dio or raw response DTOs.

`API response → ClaimModel → ClaimEntity → UseCase → BLoC → UI`

## Status mapping

Never show raw backend status strings in UI. Map in Domain, localize in Presentation.

```text
Backend: CORRECTION_REQUIRED
Domain:  ClaimStatus.correctionRequired
UI:      l10n (Correction Required / مطلوب تصحيح)
```

If backend status values change, update the mapping layer only.

## UI contracts for API-driven states

- Localize all loading/error/empty/validation/success/status copy (Arabic RTL, English LTR). No hardcoded user-facing strings.
- Light and dark mode via existing theme (`context.colors`). No hardcoded feature colors.
- Layout via `AppSizes` (`context.space*`, `context.width`, `context.height`). See the AppSizes rule.
